{"title":"2019 BmMT Individual Problems","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div style=\"border: 1px solid #444; background: #fff; max-width: 600px; margin: 0 auto 20px auto; font-size: 90%; line-height: 1.6; font-family: sans-serif;\">\n<div style=\"background: #e0dbff; padding: 12px; text-align: center; border-bottom: 1px solid #444;\">\n<p><span style=\"font-size: 110%; font-weight: bold; color: #4b3ba7;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_BmMT_Individual_(Answer_Key)&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2019 BmMT Individual (Answer Key) (page does not exist)\">2019 BmMT Individual (Answer Key)</a></span><br />\n<span style=\"font-size: 95%; color: #6c5cb8;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Berkeley_Mini_Math_Tournament&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Berkeley Mini Math Tournament (page does not exist)\">BmMT Resources</a> • <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Special:Upload&amp;wpDestFile=2019_BmMT_Individual.pdf\" class=\"new\" title=\"2019 BmMT Individual.pdf\">PDF</a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"padding: 15px 25px 15px 25px;\">\n<p style=\"font-weight: bold; margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 8px;\">Instructions</p>\n<ol style=\"margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 15px; padding-left: 20px;\">\n<li style=\"margin-bottom: 5px;\">This test contains 20 short answer questions. All answers must be expressed in simplest form unless specified otherwise. Only answers written inside the boxes on the answer sheet will be considered for grading.</li>\n<li style=\"margin-bottom: 5px;\">Each correct answer is worth 1 point. Each incorrect or blank answer is worth 0 points.</li>\n<li style=\"margin-bottom: 5px;\">No calculators are permitted. Protractors, rulers, and compasses are permitted.</li>\n<li style=\"margin-bottom: 5px;\">Figures are not necessarily drawn to scale.</li>\n<li style=\"margin-bottom: 5px;\">You will have <b>60 minutes</b> working time to complete the test.</li>\n</ol>\n<div style=\"text-align: center; border-top: 1px solid #eee; padding-top: 12px; font-weight: bold; word-spacing: 2px;\">\n<p><a href=\"#Problem_1\">1</a> • <a href=\"#Problem_2\">2</a> • <a href=\"#Problem_3\">3</a> • <a href=\"#Problem_4\">4</a> • <a href=\"#Problem_5\">5</a> • <a href=\"#Problem_6\">6</a> • <a href=\"#Problem_7\">7</a> • <a href=\"#Problem_8\">8</a> • <a href=\"#Problem_9\">9</a> • <a href=\"#Problem_10\">10</a> • <a href=\"#Problem_11\">11</a> • <a href=\"#Problem_12\">12</a> • <a href=\"#Problem_13\">13</a> • <a href=\"#Problem_14\">14</a> • <a href=\"#Problem_15\">15</a> • <a href=\"#Problem_16\">16</a> • <a href=\"#Problem_17\">17</a> • <a href=\"#Problem_18\">18</a> • <a href=\"#Problem_19\">19</a> • <a href=\"#Problem_20\">20</a>\n</p>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Problem_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Problem_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Problem_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Problem_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Problem_6\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 6</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Problem_7\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 7</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Problem_8\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 8</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Problem_9\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 9</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Problem_10\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 10</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#Problem_11\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">11</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 11</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-12\"><a href=\"#Problem_12\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">12</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 12</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-13\"><a href=\"#Problem_13\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">13</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 13</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-14\"><a href=\"#Problem_14\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">14</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 14</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-15\"><a href=\"#Problem_15\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">15</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 15</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-16\"><a href=\"#Problem_16\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">16</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 16</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-17\"><a href=\"#Problem_17\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">17</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 17</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-18\"><a href=\"#Problem_18\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">18</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 18</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-19\"><a href=\"#Problem_19\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">19</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 19</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-20\"><a href=\"#Problem_20\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">20</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 20</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-21\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">21</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_1\">Problem 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_BmMT_Individual_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If Clark wants to divide <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/9/e59e2c6e83eb78cca610a5fd4070ae01c8d4ae60.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> pizzas among <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/6/66644fd9f411299c3c1eabf151b5f601c9ef6c21.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$25$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> people so that each person receives the same number of pizzas, how many pizzas should each person receive?\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_BmMT_Individual_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2019 BmMT Individual Problems/Problem 1\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_2\">Problem 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_BmMT_Individual_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In a group of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> people, every pair of people shakes hands once. How many handshakes occur?\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_BmMT_Individual_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2019 BmMT Individual Problems/Problem 2\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_3\">Problem 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_BmMT_Individual_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Dylan and Joey have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/0/820a20de2847dfdc1bc5cffc8d904933150032bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$14$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> costumes in total. Dylan gives Joey <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> costumes, and Joey now has the number of costumes that Dylan had before giving Joey any costumes. How many costumes does Dylan have now?\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_BmMT_Individual_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2019 BmMT Individual Problems/Problem 3\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_4\">Problem 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_BmMT_Individual_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>At Banjo Borger, a burger costs <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> dollars, a soda costs <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> dollars, and a cookie costs <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> dollars. Alex, Connor, and Tony each spent <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/8/c6878713578626763c38433b3f4c8c2205ad0c15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> dollars on their order, but none of them got the same order. If Connor bought the most cookies, how many cookies did Connor buy?\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_BmMT_Individual_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2019 BmMT Individual Problems/Problem 4\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_5\">Problem 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_BmMT_Individual_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Joey, James, and Austin stand on a large, flat field. If the distance from Joey to James is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/1/651ba418a810d971dbc8a326d49a71fe1541fae0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> and the distance from Austin to James is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/7/5e7a1b6098a8c98b8e4adae526aeef4b91712620.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$18$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, what is the minimal possible distance from Joey to Austin?\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_BmMT_Individual_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2019 BmMT Individual Problems/Problem 5 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_6\">Problem 6</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_BmMT_Individual_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 6\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If the first and third terms of a five-term arithmetic sequence are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, respectively, what is the sum of all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> terms in the sequence.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_BmMT_Individual_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2019 BmMT Individual Problems/Problem 6 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_7\">Problem 7</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_BmMT_Individual_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 7\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>What is the area of the S-shaped figure below, which has constant vertical height <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and width <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />?\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2019_BmMT_Individual_Problems&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_BmMT_Individual_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2019 BmMT Individual Problems/Problem 7 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_8\">Problem 8</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_BmMT_Individual_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 8\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If the side length of square <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, what is the perimeter of square <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />, formed by connecting the midpoints of the sides of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />?\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_BmMT_Individual_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2019 BmMT Individual Problems/Problem 8 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_9\">Problem 9</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_BmMT_Individual_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 9\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The Chan Shun Auditorium at UC Berkeley has room number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/e/b5e9d05638a84f9dcdf11f64270d5e96419740e4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2050$\" width=\"35\" height=\"12\" />. The number of the seats in the auditorium is a factor of the room number, and there are between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/e/f5e10e5f3aa7c766cb27c3ad319fa526f71588cd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$150$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/6/c96cf089c5adcb3126fb734f52b768b3002dedce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$431$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> seats, inclusive. What is the sum of all of the possible numbers of seats in Chan Shun Auditorium?\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_BmMT_Individual_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2019 BmMT Individual Problems/Problem 9 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_10\">Problem 10</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_BmMT_Individual_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 10\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Krishna has a positive integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />. He notices that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/e/a6e87b69178d197c13b13d595e7e6817cf20df95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"17\" /> has the same last digit as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />. If Krishna knows that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> is a prime number less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/6/906734e2f1010e9a171ffee8050cbc0649cea37c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$50$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, how many possible values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> are there?\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_BmMT_Individual_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2019 BmMT Individual Problems/Problem 10\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_11\">Problem 11</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_BmMT_Individual_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=11\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 11\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Jing Jing the Kangaroo starts on the number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. If she is at a positive integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />, she can either jump to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/3/f93f5c51ea4b04b4992b003b39479f29018f6bda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2n$\" width=\"19\" height=\"12\" /> or to the sum of the digits of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />. What is the smallest positive integer she cannot reach no matter how she jumps?\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_BmMT_Individual_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2019 BmMT Individual Problems/Problem 11\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_12\">Problem 12</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_BmMT_Individual_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=12\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 12\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Sylvia is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> units directly east of Druv and runs twice as fast as Druv. When a whistle blows, Druv runs directly north, and Sylvia runs along a straight line. If they meet at a point a distance <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96ab646de7704969b91c76a214126b45f2b07b25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> units away from Druv's original location, what is the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96ab646de7704969b91c76a214126b45f2b07b25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />?\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_BmMT_Individual_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2019 BmMT Individual Problems/Problem 12\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_13\">Problem 13</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_BmMT_Individual_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=13\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 13\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> is a real number such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/c/fdcf921553a2b1e5099c8552c8757478014d1198.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{x} + \\sqrt{10} = \\sqrt{x + 20}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"173\" height=\"23\" />, compute <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_BmMT_Individual_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2019 BmMT Individual Problems/Problem 13 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_14\">Problem 14</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_BmMT_Individual_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=14\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 14\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Compute the number of rearrangements of the letters in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/0/1c09fa4958a872ffb29899c8c16142af5d5ea918.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$LATEX$\" width=\"69\" height=\"13\" /> such that the letter <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/5/2554b6496c3b678897e9b060ef00aa9f0a7d7ece.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> comes before the letter <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and the letter <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> comes before the letter <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />. For example, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/d/b7d5a603b8cb751b3dd45d2a87d4af67319043af.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$TLEAX$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"72\" height=\"14\" /> is a valid rearrangement, but <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/c/5dc84a07442481762f4e6d7fe6d927e7bc00be69.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$LAETX$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"72\" height=\"14\" /> is not.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_BmMT_Individual_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2019 BmMT Individual Problems/Problem 14\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_15\">Problem 15</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_BmMT_Individual_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=15\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 15\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>How many integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> greater than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> are there such that the degree measure of each interior angle of a regular <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />-gon is an even integer?\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_BmMT_Individual_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2019 BmMT Individual Problems/Problem 15 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_16\">Problem 16</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_BmMT_Individual_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=16\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 16\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Students are being assigned to faculty mentors in the Berkeley Math Department. If there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> students and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> mentors and each student has exactly one mentor, in how many ways can students be assigned to mentors given that each mentor has at least one student?\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_BmMT_Individual_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2019 BmMT Individual Problems/Problem 16 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_17\">Problem 17</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_BmMT_Individual_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=17\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 17\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Karthik has a paper square of side length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. He folds the square along a crease that connects the midpoints of two opposite sides (as shown in the left diagram, where the dotted line indicates the fold). He takes the resulting rectangle and folds it such that one of its vertices lands on the vertex that is diagonally opposite. Find the area of Karthik's final figure.\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2019_BmMT_Individual_Problems&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_BmMT_Individual_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2019 BmMT Individual Problems/Problem 17 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_18\">Problem 18</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_BmMT_Individual_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=18\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 18\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Sally is inside a pen consisting of points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/e/28e24c43456d95b5ab8d4f2f8f85a644e98b7ed3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a, b)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/7/0073d08b0e8b1eb0a4f4577fd54722fbd564b06b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0 \\leq a, b \\leq 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"94\" height=\"18\" />. If she is currently on the point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/f/adfd9ae8a3fac031d3b8b470a52a709a23d4d6d2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x, y)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"44\" height=\"20\" />, she can move to either <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/a/a4ad0bcb15c2b5c0bd1f5009772733672341ae7e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x, y + 1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"75\" height=\"20\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/1/aa159683250c458e150a51bb6ff90e60f479c288.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x, y - 1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"75\" height=\"20\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/c/87c68e46d0751179bf4b194982e5a155a852748f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x + 1, y)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"72\" height=\"18\" />. Given that she cannot revisit any point she has visited before, find the number of ways she can reach <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/a/79ad99fd4eff7c80182e09559fe59f36b5844e2a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(4, 4)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" /> from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/b/c4b86f54134d69cad8793688a431aa907aaf2698.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(0, 0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"42\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_BmMT_Individual_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2019 BmMT Individual Problems/Problem 18 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_19\">Problem 19</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_BmMT_Individual_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=19\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 19\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>An ant sits on the circumference of the circular base of a party hat (a cone without a circular base for the ant to walk on) of radius <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and height <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/e/82e93b4bff537e8b63a0a3db030fbb756ab27255.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"24\" height=\"18\" />. If the ant wants to reach a point diametrically opposite of its current location on the hat, what is the minimum possible distance the ant needs to travel.\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2019_BmMT_Individual_Problems&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_BmMT_Individual_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2019 BmMT Individual Problems/Problem 19 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_20\">Problem 20</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_BmMT_Individual_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=20\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 20\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If\n</p>\n<center><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/6/9e6fc3a0a3c0edfa0a9fe93d5e816b69a9db39ca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)=\\frac{2^{19}x + 2^{20}}{x^{2} + 2^{20}x + 2^{20}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"184\" height=\"42\" /></center><p>,\n</p><p>find the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/4/ba40315906f1767b33b5410fc19e6507d3649281.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(1) + f(2) + f(4) + f(8) + \\cdots + f(2^{20})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"319\" height=\"21\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_BmMT_Individual_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2019 BmMT Individual Problems/Problem 20 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_BmMT_Individual_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=21\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Template:BmMT_Individual_box&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Template:BmMT Individual box (page does not exist)\">Template:BmMT Individual box</a>\n</p>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Berkeley_Mini_Math_Tournament&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Berkeley Mini Math Tournament (page does not exist)\">Berkeley Mini Math Tournament</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=BmMT_Problems_and_Solutions&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"BmMT Problems and Solutions (page does not exist)\">BmMT Problems and Solutions</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mathematics_competitions\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Mathematics competitions\">Mathematics competitions</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mathematics_competition_resources\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Mathematics competition resources\">Mathematics competition resources</a></li></ul>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018062401\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.060 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.122 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 456/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 963/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 11100/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   17.782      1 -total\n 43.52%    7.738      3 Template:Image_needed\n 16.90%    3.005      1 Template:BmMT_Individual_box\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:37867:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018062401 and revision id 292578. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}